Package: cuems-nodeconf
Version: 0.1.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>
Installed-Size: 153
Depends: cuems-utils (>= 0.1.0rc5), cuems-common (>= 1.0.0), python3 (>= 3.11), python3-netifaces, python3-dbus, python3-zeroconf, python3-systemd (>= 235), avahi-daemon, avahi-utils
Section: python
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/stagesoft/cuems-nodeconf
Description: CUEMS node discovery + adoption daemon
 cuems-nodeconf discovers CUEMS cluster nodes over avahi/zeroconf
 (_cuems_nodeconf._tcp), elects controller vs node role, and maintains
 /etc/cuems/network_map.xml (uuid, mac, ip, node_type, adopted, online)
 as nodes appear and their IPv4LL addresses change.
 .
 On the controller it also publishes interface-scoped avahi aliases via the
 D-Bus EntryGroup API: controller.local on the cluster interface and a UI
 alias on the outward-facing interface. Scoping each A record to a single
 interface avoids leaking the link-local cluster address onto the UI network
 (RFC 6762 section 6.2).
 .
 This package installs into the /usr/lib/cuems/ virtual environment provided
 by cuems-utils. The console script is installed at
 /usr/lib/cuems/bin/cuems-nodeconf and is invoked by the systemd unit shipped
 in cuems-common.
